# Two Joy-Cons under padmate's default, COMBINE=0 (IN-07, ADR-0022):
# each is its own gamepad. Joy-Con (L) holds east. Joy-Con (R) wakes
# while L has the slot: with one slot it waits, and its tap of south
# maps nothing (multi-joycon gives it a second slot). L lets go of east,
# so it holds nothing when it is switched off and SDL has no recentering
# ButtonUp to send. R stands in at once, provisionally, and its south
# taps Ctrl+Z.
# The GUIDs are made up in the layout of SDL's HIDAPI GUIDs: Bluetooth,
# CRC 0, Nintendo's 057e with product 2006 or 2007, and an arbitrary last
# byte. The serials are made-up MACs; the paths are left empty, since the
# key of a gamepad with a serial does not use them.
